=== 6. Both drm_driver instances report 0.6.0 in the built object ===
# struct drm_driver { int major; int minor; int patchlevel; ... } - the DWARF
# member offsets below are from readelf --debug-dump=info on the built .ko.
$ readelf --debug-dump=info src/sm750hdmidrm.ko | <member offsets>
major     <183b7>   DW_AT_data_member_location: 136
minor     <183c6>   DW_AT_data_member_location: 140
patchlevel     <183d5>   DW_AT_data_member_location: 144

$ objdump -s -j .rodata --start-address=0x840 --stop-address=0x870 src/sm750hdmidrm.ko   # shadow driver
Contents of section .rodata:
 0840 00000000 00000000 00000000 06000000  ................
 0850 00000000 00000000 00000000 00000000  ................
 0860 00000000 00000000 13000000 00000000  ................
$ objdump -s -j .rodata --start-address=0x920 --stop-address=0x950 src/sm750hdmidrm.ko   # TTM driver
Contents of section .rodata:
 0920 00000000 00000000 00000000 06000000  ................
 0930 00000000 00000000 00000000 00000000  ................
 0940 00000000 00000000 13000000 00000000  ................
# major/minor/patchlevel sit at struct offsets 136/140/144 (0x88/0x8c/0x90) in
# this build: 0x7c0+0x88 = 0x848 and 0x8a0+0x88 = 0x928 hold major, and the
# bytes at 0x84c / 0x92c are 06000000 and 06000000 -> minor = 6 in BOTH
# instances. The driver therefore reports 0.6.0 to modetest.

